&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who/What is Artefact?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming&amp;nbsp;organizations through data and AI. We combine the rigor of top-tier strategy consulting&amp;nbsp;with deep expertise in data, digital, and analytics to help clients achieve tangible&lt;br&gt;business impact.&lt;br&gt;With 1,800+ consultants, data scientists, and engineers across 23 countries, we work&amp;nbsp;with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange, and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is&amp;nbsp;at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic&amp;nbsp;challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and&amp;nbsp;new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are looking for a Senior Data &amp;amp; AI Architect who combines business strategy and technology across Data and GenAI. You will design the operating model and the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE, define the target architecture, and steer data products from demand through to rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model and organization&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design the Data &amp;amp; AI operating model (centralized, federated, hub-and-spoke) following Data Mesh principles: roles, responsibilities, domain ownership and governance mechanisms.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE: scope, service catalogue, skills, sizing and engagement model with business domains.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design end-to-end processes for demand management, use case prioritization, funding and value tracking.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Architecture and technology choices&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the target data platform architecture on cloud (Azure, AWS, GCP) and Databricks, including GenAI components (RAG, agents, vector stores, LLMOps).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Run make-or-buy analyses and vendor selections: scouting, evaluation criteria, business case, TCO and final recommendation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Check that architecture, security and data governance choices are consistent with enterprise standards and with the operating model.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data products: from demand to rollout&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Gather and formalize functional requirements with the business, translating them into data products with owners, consumers, SLAs and quality metrics.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design data products from both a functional angle (use cases, KPIs, impacted processes) and a technical one (data model, pipelines, interfaces, serving layer).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as design authority during implementation: review system integrator solutions and oversee quality, progress and risks of the rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 4 years of professional experience in IT.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 2 years on projects focused on AI/GenAI, Data Mesh and functional requirements gathering.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Consulting experience, ideally in strategy consulting, combined with experience at a system integrator or delivery firm.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hands-on experience designing operating models, Data/AI organizations or CoEs.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience with make-or-buy analyses, vendor selection or target architecture definition.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent written and spoken English.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Technical and functional skills:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will not be expected to write code, but you need to know the technologies well enough to assess them, challenge vendors and spot a flawed setup.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data Mesh and governance: domain ownership, data products, federated governance, data contracts, catalogues and lineage (e.g. Unity Catalog, OpenMetadata, Collibra).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cloud: data and AI PaaS services on at least one of Azure, AWS and GCP; security, networking and FinOps principles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Databricks: Lakehouse, Delta Lake, Unity Catalog, Workflows; ability to assess design and cost.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;GenAI: RAG and agentic architectures, LLMOps, model evaluation, platforms such as Azure AI Foundry, Vertex AI and Bedrock.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model: Data/AI organization, CoE, roles (data owner, data steward, product owner), demand and portfolio processes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Requirements and delivery: requirements gathering, user stories, process modelling, agile methods, programme governance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Business: business cases, TCO, value tracking, and the ability to translate technical choices into economic impact.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
